{
  "$comment": "The built-in connection kinds World Hub publishes under. This file is the source: migration 012 seeds a frozen copy of it, tests/vocabulary.test.mjs asserts the rows that migration creates still match what is written here, and the consumer kit ships it so an application can read a canonical fact without hard-coding a label. A package also carries catalog/connection-kinds.json describing every kind it actually uses, built-in and custom alike, so a setting-specific kind needs no consumer change at all. Bump connectionKindsVersion whenever a kind is renamed or retired, and add the new kind in a new numbered migration rather than editing 012 — a migration that seeded from this file would seed different rows on replay.",
  "connectionKindsVersion": 1,

  "categories": [
    { "id": "social", "label": "People", "section": "People" },
    { "id": "affiliation", "label": "Affiliations", "section": "Affiliations" },
    { "id": "place", "label": "Places", "section": "Places" },
    { "id": "identity", "label": "Identity", "section": "Identity" },
    { "id": "ownership", "label": "Objects", "section": "Objects" },
