    { "id": "organization", "label": "Organizations", "section": "Groups" },
    { "id": "subject", "label": "Subjects", "section": "Subjects" },
    { "id": "legacy", "label": "Older connections", "section": "Other connections" }
  ],

  "$comment_kinds": "forwardLabel and forwardSection are what the source record's own page shows; inverseLabel and inverseSection are what the counterpart's page shows. A symmetric kind reads the same from both sides. `sentence` is the fact stated plainly, used by the authoring drawer so an author confirms a sentence rather than a direction. `pairs` are the ordered (source type, target type) combinations the kind allows — the orientation of a new connection is read from here, never chosen by hand.",

